-where $G(\mathbf{abcd}) = G(\mathbf{a}, \mathbf{b})G(\mathbf{b}, \mathbf{c})G(\mathbf{c}, \mathbf{d})$ and $\rho(\mathbf{abc}) = \rho(\mathbf{a})\rho(\mathbf{b})\rho(\mathbf{c})$. The term $\rho(\mathbf{d})$ is excluded because the outgoing direction $\omega_{dc}$ and incident direction at $\mathbf{d}$ are given as input [S1]. $C_\Xi$ is a normalization factor dependent on the configuration [S1].
+**Target PDF**
+The goal is to sample $\mathbf{b}$ and $t_{dc}$ from a joint distribution proportional to the geometry and scattering terms:
+$$ p(\mathbf{b}, t_{dc} \mid \Xi) G(\mathbf{c}, \mathbf{d}) = C_\Xi G(\mathbf{abcd}) \rho(\mathbf{abc}) $$
+where $C_\Xi$ is a normalization factor dependent on the input configuration $\Xi = \{\mathbf{a}, \boldsymbol{\omega}_{la}, \mathbf{d}, \boldsymbol{\omega}_{dc}\}$ [S1].
 
-**Factorizations:**
